cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HSRI data or methodology, please cite as below."
type: dataset
title: "Human Superintelligence Readiness Index (HSRI)"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
url: "https://krish-rm.github.io/hsri-research/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/krish-rm/hsri-research"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >
  The Sovereign Human Agency Imperative: An Empirical Benchmark, Psychometric Foundation,
  and Transition Evidence Map for National Preparedness in the Era of Advanced AI.
  Synthesizes 780 macro observations across 39 nations, a 9-paradigm behavioral experiment battery
  (N=1,080), 4-factor latent CFA (incremental validity Delta R^2 = +0.4870), cross-cultural scalar invariance
  (N=2,000), longitudinal stability (N=600), 7-provider frontier multi-agent consensus, in-situ operator
  oversight across 4 sectors, OECD/JRC 7-step composite audit, dynamic Kalman filtering, and ASI transition simulation batteries.
authors:
  - name: "HSRI Research Consortium"
keywords:
  - AI readiness
  - human-AI interaction
  - cognitive discernment
  - automation bias
  - psychometrics
  - benchmark
  - superintelligence
